
# [<tag>] <subject> (Max 70 char)
# |<----   Preferably using up to 60 chars   --->|<------------------->|
# Example: [feature] Implement automated commit messages

# (Optional) Explain why this change is being made
# |<----   Try To Limit Each Line to a Maximum Of 70-75 Characters   ---->|

# --- COMMIT END ---
# Tag can be
#    ci            (CI/CD related changes)
#    doc           (Changes to documentation)
#    feat          (New feature)
#    fix           (Bug fix)
#    nfc           (Refactoring code)
#    test          (Adding or refactoring tests; no production code change)
#    version       (Version bump/new release; no production code change)
#
# Note: Multiple tags can be combined, e.g. [feat][server] Save and load filters in the GUI
# --------------------
# Remember to:
#   * The commit message description should contain the issue number (Either GitHub or Jira) and a short
#     description of the problem. Follow the GitHub conventions e.g. fixes #<issue_number>.
#   * Capitalize the subject line.
#   * Use the imperative mode in the subject line.
#   * Do not end the subject line with a period.
#   * Separate subject from body with a blank line.
#   * Use the body to explain what and why vs how.
#   * Can use multiple lines with "-" or "*" for bullet points in body.
# --------------------
